{"title":"A Knight to Die For","intro":"Hear ye, hear ye! A royal feast is upon us. Nobles and peasants alike are called to a night of revelry and merriment in Moffett Keep, the ancestral seat of the Vale of Silicon. Drama and castle intrigue abound, and as the night grows longer, who knows what may happen... and who will make it out alive...","iter":310000,"characters":[{"id":"bayesford","name":"Lady Cleo Bayesford","description":"The widowed Duchess of Monterey who has ruled the bayside keep since her husband disappeared in the Southern Wastes two years ago.","image":"images/bayesford.png","base":{"s":"e85/mtpq6AA0NfHz/Oor6g==","i":"T5QiKTqVqvoxO+ym","c":""}},{"id":"motley","name":"Pippa Motley","description":"The most recent court jester to terrorize the halls of Moffett Keep, hoping to outdo - and outlast - her predecessor.","image":"images/jester.png","base":{"s":"jR81l8x4EQI3jkiImmfsVQ==","i":"AJzxtHFLl685r0aE","c":""}},{"id":"silas","name":"Lord Silas Ameswyck","description":"The Duke of Modesto and younger brother of King Godfrey Ameswyck, who helped his rise to power and oversees the food supply for Moffett Keep.","image":"images/ameswyck_fruit.png","base":{"s":"+ZD8XibKKSdI1gNQD9ymLQ==","i":"lQoc/TcdyQGLcf5m","c":""}},{"id":"quill","name":"Mistress Cecily Quill","description":"The Royal Scholar, in charge of recordkeeping and histories but also keen on learning the workings of the mysterious ancient buildings on the bayshore.","image":"images/scholar.png","base":{"s":"YjZg25Xfb6pFbd8ZkkHkvA==","i":"I+n5TdMAZZRsYiOh","c":""}},{"id":"vortigan","name":"Lady Elinor Vortigan","description":"The King's trusted Advisor, who has been at court for his entire rule and has been instrumental in securing stability in the Vale of Silicon.","image":"images/vortigan.png","base":{"s":"KJYtZG8uIJOR17rV4De/cA==","i":"M/Y0lP+XG0iq/pxi","c":""}},{"id":"king","name":"King Godfrey Ameswyck, Third of His Name, Purveyor of Mountains and Protector of the Bay","description":"The ruler of the Vale of Silicon who consolidated power over the region five years ago.","image":"images/ameswyck_crown.png","base":{"s":"DQmcGoQn8nNmSDdg0MzKag==","i":"tXLrzn2ufoH5dS1P","c":""}},{"id":"faradayne","name":"Elsbeth Faradayne","description":"The local apothecary who is a not uncommon sight in the halls of Moffett Keep.","image":"images/apothecary.png","base":{"s":"+vo+KnBk8sNUGxNBJp4URg==","i":"jf3nGnJN+t//n/Mu","c":""}},{"id":"tamal","name":"Tamal, Bringer of Fog, the Witch of Muir","description":"A figure shrouded in mystery, you deal in the occult from your domain to the north of The Bridge.","image":"images/muir.png","base":{"s":"UnSgxlxY5SRnqcBfdIDtnQ==","i":"CkHtj8yMnMFujUQY","c":""}},{"id":"kalman","name":"Sir Kalman the Unerring","description":"A newcomer to Moffett Keep who earned his knighthood when he defeated Lord Aldric in a tournament.","image":"images/knight.png","base":{"s":"lfWfLyPicSw3dKi+oc5PdQ==","i":"IQ2eI2W2IZERq8vU","c":""}},{"id":"cassandra","name":"Princess Cassandra Ameswyck","description":"The princess of Moffett Keep who spends a lot of time studying with Mistress Cecily.","image":"images/ameswyck.png","base":{"s":"AX8QPDVCcO00WBLIgd/wBg==","i":"Sx6S/JFZU8xys9lC","c":""}},{"id":"aeolia","name":"Aeolia, High Priestess of the Wind","description":"High Priestess of the Wind Priestesses, an obscure group that keeps to themselves.","image":"images/wind.png","base":{"s":"PrgC4Z0Jue5HajogX09+Nw==","i":"RsbYPKsFkI/AClWZ","c":""}}]}